1.Explain the role of providers, resources, data sources, variables, locals, and outputs.
Provider: plugin that talks to an API (e.g., hashicorp/aws).
Resource: creates/updates infra.
Data source: reads existing data (no changes).
Variables/locals: inputs & computed helpers.
Outputs: export values for calling modules/CI.

2.count vs for_each—when and why?
count uses index-based addressing; changes in order can force recreation.
for_each uses stable keys; safer for sets/maps; better lifecycle stability.

